title: Pinboard
tags: Plugins Engines
icon: $:/core/images/layout-button
builds-upon: Graph

Pinboard is an engine for <<.graph>> that turns a graph into an ''infinite canvas'' for thinking and presenting. Nodes become cards showing the fields you choose, you can draw, write and place shapes around them, and a path of frames, cards and views plays back as a fullscreen presentation where the camera flies across the board.

<$boundingbox width=100% height=560px>

<$graph.view $tiddler="$:/graph/Pinboard Demo" />

</$boundingbox>

Try it: drag cards, hover a card for its tools (view, open, fields, add to path), double-click a card to read it in the full-height viewer, pick a pen or shape from the dock, then press ▶ (top right).

! Pros

* Cards render real tiddler content: wikitext, links, transclusions, images and tags, at any zoom level.
* Per-card choice of shown fields and their order, stored with the board.
* Vector drawing layer: pen, highlighter, rectangles, ellipses, lines, arrows, text, sticky notes, frames. Undo/redo.
* Presentation mode with smooth zoom-and-pan flights between stops.
* No third-party library; small and fast for boards of a few hundred cards.

! Cons

* No physics or automatic layout. Unpositioned cards are laid out on a grid.
* Experimental.

! Installation

Drag this pill onto your wiki along with <<.graph>>:

@@text-align:center;
<$link to="$:/plugins/lasjoh-toho/pinboard" class="graph-dragger graph-dragger-engine">{{$:/core/images/layout-button}}<br>Pinboard</$link>
@@

Then pick the template ''Pinboard (infinite canvas & presentation)'' in a graph's settings.

